hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1154","Yusuf bin Musa narrated to us, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Al-Amash, H. Abu Musa narrated to us, and Ya’qub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman narrated to us. On the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, he said: Abdullah bin Masoud said: “I prayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and in a hadith Al-Thawri: One night, and they said: He went on for so long that I was thinking about something bad. It was said: And what was I thinking about? He said: “I was about to sit down and call him.”"
"1155","Abu Hashim Ziyad bin Ayyub narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah and Ya’la narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, h. Salam bin Junada narrated to us, he narrated to us Waki’, on the authority of Al-Amash, H. Ibrahim bin Bastam Al-Zaafrani narrated to us, Abu Ali Al-Hanafi narrated to us, Malik bin Mughul narrated to us, he said: Al-Amash told me, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked: Which prayer is best? He said: “The length of Qunoot.”"
